    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**1. Governance Export Issue** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n- Kept the default export intact for backward compatibility\n\n**2. Toxicity Metric Bug** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n- Wrapped `toxicityMetric` in DEFAULT_METRICS to filter out the references parameter\n- The issue: `runEvaluations` passes both outputs and references to all metrics, but `toxicityMetric` was interpreting the references as banned terms\n- With the old code, 'Hello' matched 'hello' (from references) and 'friendly world' matched itself, flagging both as toxic (score 0)\n- With the fix, `toxicityMetric` only receives outputs and uses the default banned terms, correctly scoring 1 (no toxic content)\n\nAll 28 tests now pass successfully.",
